================================================================================
LINUX VALIDATION + 16-CORE SCALING: internal-MPI mpi-cpu on gpudyn3
================================================================================
Date     : 2026-06-11
Branch   : mpi-parallel (origin, post-C1 be3dd39)
Host     : gpudyn3 -- Ubuntu, 2x Xeon Silver 4309Y (16 physical cores, SMT2 ->
           nproc 32), 125 GB, system Open MPI 4.1.2 (/usr/bin/mpirun; no conda
           env needed). Binary: GPU2/run_ampere/nbody7b.mpi-cpu (local
           RUNDIR=run_ampere Makefile tweak).
Baseline : results_c1_gpupot_2026-06-10.log (Mac M4 Pro, np<=8)

PORTING FIXES (harness-only; no integrator code touched)
  1. fort.10 case bug: the harnesses staged the IC file as `Fort.10`, but
     READ (10,*) in Block/data.f binds to gfortran's implicit unit-10 name,
     lowercase `fort.10`. The Mac's case-insensitive FS masked this; on Linux
     every rank opened a freshly created EMPTY fort.10 and died at EOF
     (data.f:78). All four harnesses now stage the file as lowercase fort.10
     (identical resolution on the Mac).
  2. Hardcoded Mac paths: ROOT is now derived from the script location
     (overridable via ROOT=), and BIN auto-detected under GPU2/run_*/
     (overridable via BIN=), so run_versions vs run_ampere both work.
  3. run_equiv.sh: FAIL early if the np1 reference itself is empty
     (previously an np1 crash surfaced as confusing per-rank EMPTY lines).
  4. extract() in run_equiv.sh / run_io_guard.sh now also strips the
     CPUTOT/WTOT accumulators from the END RUN line -- on the Mac they
     matched only by rounding luck.
  (Execute bits on the *.sh were lost in the pull; chmod +x restored.)

BIT-IDENTITY (gate before any timing)
  run_equiv.sh (13049-body BSE, per-rank dirs) : PASS -- np1/2/4, all ranks.
  run_io_guard.sh (shared dir, guard ON, np4)  : PASS -- physics lines and
    every output file byte-identical to the np1 reference (fort.1/fort.2:
    same size, 12 differing bytes = timing fields, as documented).
  N=5e4 attribution runs: np8/np16/np32 ADJUST + END RUN physics lines
    bit-identical to np1 at both cadences (timer fields stripped).

